In commit "mining: handle negative and NaN waitTipChanged timeouts" (758ae2c916eb8d2127ab1949b9630cf4348b8945)

nit: could say why the comparison is negated, here and in `waitTipChanged`, so it doesn't get simplified to `timeout < 0ms`, which would accept NaN:

```cpp
// Timeout can come from an IPC client, so reject negative and NaN values.
// The negated comparison is also true for NaN.
```

